[IMP] product, mrp, sale, sale_pdf_quote_builder, website_sale: Documents management improvement

The goal of this PR is to improve the usage of documents linked to a product.

When the website_sale module is installed, the “Publish On Website” field
used to display documents on the product page in the eCommerce) has been
merged into the “attached_on_sale” selection field. When this field is selected,
it behaves the same as selecting “From quotation”, with the additional feature
of displaying the documents on the product page in the eCommerce.

When accessing documents linked to a product, it is now possible to enable
the “On Product Page” field for a specific variant, allowing documents
related to that variant to be displayed on its eCommerce page.

When accessing the Quotation Builder from a Sales Order,
documents are always selectable. Since the default quote builder
includes all documents, the filter on PDFs has been moved to
the PDF rendering stage.

In Quote Builder PDF "On Product Page" and "Never" are before the quotation
and "From Quotation" and "On Order Confirmation" are after the quotation.

The following UI improvements have been made:
* Removed the PDF icon from the document kanban view
* On the eCommerce product page, the “Documents” title now uses
  the same style and position as other section headers
* Added Sales pages to the document edit view
* Document titles are no longer truncated in the kanban view
* “Variants” ribbons have been replaced with tags
* The button to configure PDF forms has been redesigned and is displayed conditionally
* Some fields have been renamed and moved

